{
  // Coodsz community mod compatibility list.
  // Coodsz Host and Coodsz Coop and Friends download this file and show a badge next to each mod
  // (Works, Broken, Client only or Unknown). Without internet they use the last copy they downloaded,
  // and the copy built into the tools when there is none.
  //
  // Fields:
  //   id        Module Id from the mod's SubModule.xml (<Id value="..."/>). This is what the tools match on.
  //   name      Display name.
  //   status    "Unknown" | "Works" | "Broken" | "ClientOnly"
  //             A hand kept "Works" whose note starts with "Works with issues." runs with the fixes the note gives.
  //   coop      Coop version a hand written verdict was checked with. Entries with "coop" are kept by hand:
  //             the automatic tally updates their counts but never their status.
  //   note      Short explanation shown with the badge.
  //   workshop  Steam Workshop item id (steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=...).
  //   nexus     Nexus Mods mod id (nexusmods.com/mountandblade2bannerlord/mods/...).
  //   category  Framework | Gameplay | Overhaul | Troops | Items | UI | Graphics | Audio | Map | Characters | Utility
  //   works     Number of people who reported "works".
  //   broken    Number of people who reported "broken".
  //   clientOnly  Number of people who reported "client-only" (only when there are any; it never changes the status).
  //   lastReport  The day of the newest counted report, YYYY-MM-DD (only on reported mods).
  //   idGuess   true when the real Module Id is not known yet and "id" is just the display name.
  //             The first report that carries both the real id and this name fixes it automatically.
  //
  // Seeded from CoopKeep's list (https://github.com/Aderimo/bannerlord-coopkeep, MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 aderimo):
  // the most subscribed Steam Workshop and most downloaded Nexus Mods Bannerlord mods, most still "Unknown".
  // The hand entries come from the Coodsz tools' own notes (the Coodsz Host working list, the TAOM list and
  // the server module notes) and from Coop's Server Instructions.md (War Sails, Birth and Aging Options, Fast Mode).
  // Coodsz's Coop 0.1.6 compatibility thread on Discord (2026-10-08, edited 2026-10-14) added the verdicts whose
  // note names it as the source; most of those were tested on Coop 0.1.5 and wait for a retest.
  //
  // Automation (.github/workflows/mod-compat-tally.yml):
  //   Every "Mod compatibility" issue (label "mod-compat") is counted from scratch on each change.
  //   Issues labelled "invalid" or "spam" are ignored, and only a person's latest report per mod counts.
  //   "client-only" reports only count in "clientOnly"; the maintainer sets "ClientOnly" by hand.
  //   works - broken >= 3  -> "Works",  broken - works >= 3  -> "Broken",  otherwise the status stays.
  //   A reported mod that is not in the list is added as a new entry.
  //   The script keeps this comment block and rewrites the "mods" array, one entry per line, sorted by name.
  //   It also writes MODS.md in the repository root, the readable page of this list (the tools' Full mod list link).
